# Citation metadata for WormScan.
#
# GitHub reads this file and shows a "Cite this repository" button; Zenodo and
# most reference managers read it too. Copyright in the code belongs to Erasmus
# MC (Dutch Auteurswet art. 7, employer ownership); authorship of the work is a
# separate matter and is recorded here.
#
# CHECK BEFORE PUBLISHING: the spelling of your name, and add your ORCID.
# When the paper is out, uncomment the preferred-citation block at the bottom
# so citations point at the paper rather than the repository.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WormScan in work that is published, please cite it."
title: "WormScan: an automated imaging and analysis platform for C. elegans assays"
abstract: >-
  An imaging rig and analysis chain for C. elegans experiments. A Raspberry Pi
  with an HQ camera captures whole-plate stills and video; a Windows application
  mirrors the data and runs four analysis pipelines: swimming motility and
  crawling locomotion via Tierpsy Tracker, clonogenic colony counting, and
  developmental staging from a YOLO model.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Haeckes
    given-names: David
    affiliation: "Erasmus MC, University Medical Center Rotterdam"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/davidtheadmin/celegans-imaging"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - C. elegans
  - motility
  - developmental staging
  - image analysis
  - Raspberry Pi
  - open-source instrumentation

